 ## Background
-Sm2D was introduced in a 2012 thesis by Dirk Sowinski as part of research on real-time smoke volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. It serves as a simplified 2D test case to evaluate the applicability of texture-based approaches for smoke volumes, highlighting the trade-offs between hardware-accelerated texture sampling and explicit geometric ray tracing [S1, unofficial].
